ence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the sequence with the first four values.\n    fib_sequence = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    # Iteratively compute fib4(i) from previous four values.\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = fib_sequence[i-1] + fib_sequence[i-2] + fib_sequence[i-3] + fib_sequence[i-4]\n        fib_sequence.append(next_fib)\n\n    return fib_sequence[n]", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/47": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the median of a list of numbers. Raises ValueError if the list is empty.\"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # For an odd number of elements, return the middle element.\n        return float(sorted_l[n // 2])\n    else:\n        # For an even number of elements, return the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (float(mid1) + float(mid2)) / 2.0", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}, {"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "{\"error\": \"agent_no_response\", \"message\": \"Agent returned no response.\"}", "base_status": "fail", "plus_